 ComputeSearch←{
⍝ ⍺: unique search terms                       :: character matrix
⍝ ⍵: (weights search_columns)
⍝    weights: influence factor for each field  :: simple numeric vector
⍝    search_columns: tokenised document fields :: nested vector of character matrices, each the same width as index. ⍺≡⍥(⊢/⍴)⍵
     index←⍺ ⋄ (weights search_columns)←⍵

⍝ Tokenised best-match
⍝ Pre-compute BM25F best-match score for all tokens in corpus across all documents
⍝ BM25F shape is ≢documents × ≢terms
⍝ Zaragoza, H., Craswell, N., Taylor, M.J., Saria, S. and Robertson, S.E., 2004, November. Microsoft Cambridge at TREC 13: Web and Hard Tracks. In Trec (Vol. 4, pp. 1-1).
⍝ Then, search queries become a fast lookup into the BM25 scores table to rank relevancy

     Lookup←index∘⍳   ⍝ Cannot pass derived function across isolate boundary, so hashed Lookup function used here and recreated in main process
     search_index←Lookup¨search_columns
     term_count←¯1+↑{{≢⍵}⌸(⍳≢index)⍪⍵}¨search_index   ⍝ 3D term count: doc × field × term
     fl←≢¨search_columns                                   ⍝ Field lengths
     B←0.6                                                 ⍝ Field length normalisation parameter: 0 for none, 1 for full
     tc←term_count÷[1 2]1+B×¯1+fl÷[2](+⌿÷≢)fl              ⍝ Field length normalised term count
     tf←weights+.×2 1 3⍉tc                                 ⍝ Field-dependent normalised Term-Frequency
     rw←(⍟≢÷+⌿)+/[2]0<tc                                   ⍝ Relevance Weight (inverse document frequency for now, RSJ relevance weight in general)
    ⍝ 1+rw ensures videos still appear in results if they contain a term, even if the term doesn't affect relative ranking because it is ubiquitous
     tf(×⍤1)1+rw
 }
